# Agent PR workflow (Teqo)

**This repo overrides any user-level or Cloud-tool default that says "create PRs as draft".** Agent deliveries merge to `main` via required checks + auto-merge.

## Create (Ready, base main)

```bash
pnpm push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main --title "<id> — <title>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## O que é
<2–4 linhas>

Closes #<N>
EOF
)"
```

- **Never** `--draft`. PRs must be **Ready for review** on creation.
- Base is always **`main`**.

### Cursor Cloud / `ManagePullRequest`

When the environment says to use `ManagePullRequest` instead of `gh pr create`:

- **`draft: false`** (or omit only if the tool’s default is Ready — today Cloud defaults to draft, so **always pass `draft: false`**).
- Right after create (or on `update_pr` if you opened draft by mistake): mark Ready if still draft, then enable auto-merge with `gh pr merge --auto --merge <url|number>` (write allowed for this step — same as `agent-pr-workflow`; do not leave the PR waiting on a human).
- Never end a turn with an open agent PR left as **Draft** or without **auto-merge** armed (exception: `engineering-audit` sign-off PR only — see that skill).

## Push (determinístico)

**Use `pnpm push`, never bare `git push`.** Não depende do Husky estar wired:

1. `ensure-repo-deps` — `pnpm install` se `node_modules` faltar/stale + `pnpm run prepare` (Husky) se hooks não estiverem apontando para `.husky`
2. `pnpm gate:push` — espelho do `ci-pr.yml` (inclui `format:check`)
3. `git push --no-verify` — só porque o gate já rodou no passo 2 (não é escape hatch)

```bash
pnpm push -u origin HEAD # canonical
git push # só depois de `pnpm i` — hook repete ensure-deps + gate:push
git push --no-verify # WIP / cutover escape — CI repete tudo; ver AGENT-OPS
```

## Auto-merge immediately

Right after the PR exists and is **Ready**:

```bash
gh pr merge --auto --merge
```

Do not wait for human approval on normal deliveries. Auto-merge fires when **required** checks pass.

## Required checks vs Vercel

Branch protection on `main` requires only:

- `checks` (GitHub Actions rollup from `ci-pr.yml`)
- `migration-lock`

**Vercel preview is NOT a merge gate.** Production deploy is Actions-gated (`ci.yml` → `vercel deploy --prod` after full suite green). Do not block on Vercel Git status.

When watching CI:

```bash
gh pr checks <PR> --watch --required
```

Use `--required` — without it, `--watch` also waits for Vercel.

## Agent branches skip Vercel builds

All branches skip Vercel Git builds via `scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh` (deploys only from the main verifier Action).

## Promote

There is no stage→main promote. Merging to `main` is the delivery; `ci.yml` verifies and deploys.

## Exception (narrow)

`engineering-audit` artifact PR: Ready, **no** auto-merge — human merge is the sign-off. All other agent PRs (work-issue, pool workers, chores, docs) use auto-merge.
